  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "1 Samuel",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 14,
    "summary": "Jonathan smites the garrison of the Philistines—Saul instructs the people to eat no food until evening—Unaware of the oath, Jonathan eats, and Saul decrees his death—He is rescued by the people—Saul vexes his enemies on every hand.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Now it came to pass upon a day, that Jonathan the son of Saul said unto the young man that bare his armour, Come, and let us go over to the Philistines’ garrison, that is on the other side. But he told not his father.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 168,
            "end": 170
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 14:1",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And Saul tarried in the uttermost part of Gibeah under a pomegranate tree which is in Migron: and the people that were with him were about six hundred men;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 82
          },
          {
            "start": 114,
            "end": 118
          },
          {
            "start": 128,
            "end": 132
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 14:2",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And Ahiah, the son of Ahitub, I-chabod’s brother, the son of Phinehas, the son of Eli, the Lord’s priest in Shiloh, wearing an ephod. And the people knew not that Jonathan was gone.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 127,
            "end": 132,
            "text": "Ex. 28:4 (2–4); 1 Sam. 2:28; 22:18."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 14:3",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And between the passages, by which Jonathan sought to go over unto the Philistines’ garrison, there was a sharp rock on the one side, and a sharp rock on the other side: and the name of the one was Bozez, and the name of the other Seneh.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "1 Sam. 13:23."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 103
          },
          {
            "start": 194,
            "end": 197
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Sam. 13:23.",
            "prettyString": "1 Samuel 13:23",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1samuel",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 13,
                    "end": 13,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 23,
                        "end": 23
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 14:4",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "The forefront of the one was situate northward over against Michmash, and the other southward over against Gibeah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 28
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 14:5",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jonathan said to the young man that bare his armour, Come, and let us go over unto the garrison of these uncircumcised: it may be that the Lord will work for us: for there is no restraint to the Lord to save by many or by few.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 182,
            "end": 191,
            "text": "TG God, Power of."
          },
          {
            "start": 226,
            "end": 229,
            "text": "Judg. 7:4 (4–7)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 170,
            "end": 178
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG God, Power of.",
            "prettyString": "TG God, Power of",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
